      "content": "It is a big deal when a toddler is lethargic and shows signs of not urinating, regardless of how much they are sipping. Gatorade is not an appropriate substitute for an ORS because it can worsen diarrhea by having too much sugar. If he cannot keep down Pedialyte, try offering very small, frequent sips of electrolyte solution, perhaps even using a syringe. If he remains excessively tired or stops drinking altogether, you must seek immediate medical attention.",
